If a patient discontinues a naltrexone-treatment then every clinician should warn the patient about an overdose-risk from an opioid-use-resumption.
If a patient discontinues a naltrexone-treatment then the patient loses a previous-opioid-dosage-tolerance.
If a patient loses a previous-opioid-dosage-tolerance and the patient resumes an opioid-use then the opioid-use can possibly cause an overdose-death for the patient.
